DES (Data Encryption Standard) is a symmetric key encryption algorithm. 
 It takes 64-bit plaintext  
 Uses a 56-bit key (in real DES)  
 Performs 16 rounds  
 Uses a Feistel structure (split into Left & Right)  
our program is a simplified DES, not full DES, but follows the same idea: 
 Split data into two halves  
 Apply XOR and swapping repeatedly  
 Combine to get ciphertext 
Algorithm: 
Step 1: Initialize 64-bit plaintext 
Step 2: Split into L (32 bits) and R (32 bits) 
Step 3:Initialize key (32 bits) 
Step 4: 
Repeat 16 rounds: 
1. temp = R  
2. R = L XOR (R XOR key)  
3. L = temp 
Step 5: Combine: Cipher = R + L 
Step 6: Print encrypted output
